messages:
Ira: Heads-up  RegionalBank POC next Thurs. They want a compact SE pack: websocket streaming demo for mobile editor (low-bandwidth), function-call chaining (auth->lookup->score), NDJSON structured output for pipelines, plus a short hosted vs Dedicated 2G pricing sketch. Can someone own?

Samir: I can take the SDK + function-chain example. Clarify: chaining = model triggers lookup function, then model calls a scoring function with lookup result?

Ira: Exactly. Show auth using a service account token, how to pass limited scope to function calls, and example of graceful degradation when lookup times out.

Lydia: I'll draft the NDJSON example and the security Q&A. For NDJSON, we should show one object per line with a strict schema so their ETL can stream-parse. Also note mobile considerations: smaller chunks, resumable offsets.

Samir: Sketch (pseudo JS):

```js
// stream -> function chain
ws.send({model:'redwood-1-stream',stream:true,function_call:'auto',schema:{type:'object',properties:{type:{type:'string'},payload:{type:'object'}}}})
ws.on('function_call', async fc=>{
  if(fc.name==='auth_check'){
    const ok = await authSvc.verify(fc.args.token);
    ws.sendFunctionResult(fc.id, {ok});
  }
  if(fc.name==='lookup_customer'){
    const data = await crm.get(fc.args.id).catch(()=>null);
    ws.sendFunctionResult(fc.id, data || {error:'missing'});
  }
  if(fc.name==='score_customer'){
    const score = scoringService.score(fc.args);
    ws.sendFunctionResult(fc.id, {score});
  }
})
```

Samir: Add note: use short timeouts for mobile, send partial NDJSON lines as they arrive, and include an 'offset' field so client can resume.

Lydia: NDJSON schema example (one-line): `\{"event\":\"edit\",\"customer_id\":\"123\",\"ops\":{...}\}` - downstream can jq -c parse it. Also provide a tiny python stream parser example in the repo.

Ira: For pricing they asked hosted per-1M tokens and Dedicated 2G commit delta. Keep ballpark in one-pager; finance will confirm final numbers. Also they asked about audit logs retention and whether function-call payloads can be excluded.

Lydia: Security answers: hosted default redaction for PII; function-call payload logging can be disabled on a per-route basis; BYOK supported for Private; retention configurable up to 36 months; DPA & subprocessors link will be attached. Flagging legal for BYOK SLA.

